# <type>: (#<issue_number>) <issue_name> - <description>.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# <type> is EXACTLY one of:
#     New feature
#     Fix issue
#     Other
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Single-line, with a GitHub issue:
#     New feature: (#42) Graph export - add JSON writer for the community map.
#
# Single-line, no GitHub issue:
#     Other: bump ruff to 0.6 and reformat the data loaders.
#
# Multiline, when the change spans multiple concerns:
#     Fix issue: (#17) Pose loader crashes on empty sequence:
#     - Guard the empty-sequence branch before indexing.
#     - Add a regression test covering the zero-frame case.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Rules
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# - Single-line messages end with '.'; the first line of a multiline message
#   ends with ':'.
# - Every bullet starts with '- ' and ends with '.'.
# - Present tense, imperative mood ("add feature", not "added feature").
# - Keep commits atomic: one logical concern per commit. Split unrelated
#   changes into separate commits.
# - NEVER add trailers such as "Generated with Claude Code", author info, or
#   co-author lines.
#
# Full guidance: .github/commit_convention.md
